Description: Ask for the menus with "?lang=", not "&lang="
 The web client's bootstrap page loads the menus from
 /web/webclient/load_menus and, when the page's own address names a
 language (?lang=xx), appends it as "&lang=xx". The address has no query
 before it, so the request is /web/webclient/load_menus&lang=xx: a path
 no route matches. It answers 404, the menus never load and the web
 client does not start -- a blank page after a successful sign-in. The
 desktop opens Odoo with ?lang=, so every Odoo it opened was blank.
Author: platform-erp
Origin: other, https://github.com/OCA/OCB/blob/19.0/addons/web/views/webclient_templates.xml
Bug-Upstream: none filed
Forwarded: no
Reason: not filed yet; the same line is in odoo/odoo 19.0, where it belongs
Applied-Upstream: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
diff --git a/addons/web/views/webclient_templates.xml b/addons/web/views/webclient_templates.xml
index a34e38e..ea6c7af 100644
--- a/addons/web/views/webclient_templates.xml
+++ b/addons/web/views/webclient_templates.xml
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@
                         let menuURL = "/web/webclient/load_menus";
                         if (lang) {
                             user_context.lang = lang;
-                            menuURL += `&amp;lang=${lang}`;
+                            menuURL += `?lang=${lang}`;
                         }
                         odoo.reloadMenus = () => fetch(menuURL, { cache: "no-store" }).then(res => res.json());
                         odoo.loadMenusPromise = odoo.reloadMenus();
